# SDLC (PersonaLearn)

Follow the `sdlc-pr-lifecycle` skill for the procedure. Fill Issues and Linear issue bodies from the repo templates. PR bodies follow the `writing-prs` skill. Issue and Linear headings are in `docs/sdlc-writing-standard.md`.

## Systems

| System | Owns |
|--------|------|
| **Linear (PSL)** | Issues, status, blockers. Team: https://linear.app/personalearn/team/PSL |
| **Notion** | Specs, ADRs, release notes, retros |
| **GitHub** | Code, branches, PRs, CI, release tags |
| **Slack (#personalearn-dev)** | Notifications only |

`PSL-N` is the Linear issue identifier. A pull request that should close the issue includes `Fixes PSL-N`.

Issue → `PSL-N` → Notion spec → branch/PR → Slack. A feature or bug needs the Issue (`needs-triage`, best-guess `type-*`, assignee, milestone) before a Linear issue, a branch, or implementation.

## Branch and commit

Never implement on `develop` or `main`. Fetch `origin/develop` and branch from it, or from the merged prerequisite. Reuse an existing ticket branch.

| Work | Branch prefix | Commit prefix |
|------|---------------|---------------|
| Feature | `feature/` | `feat:` |
| Bug | `fix/` | `fix:` |
| Chore | `chore/` | `chore:` |
| Docs | `docs/` | `docs:` |

Branch: `{prefix}/PSL-{n}-{short-kebab-description}` using the Linear issue number, for example `feature/PSL-6-eval-poll-keepalive`. A production hotfix keeps the hotfix path and uses `hotfix/PSL-{n}-{short-kebab-description}`. Subject: `{prefix} … (PSL-N)`. A chore with no Linear issue yet omits `(PSL-N)` and does not invent a key. Stage only that issue’s files. Never commit secrets.

One ticket, one branch, one PR. Dependent tickets merge to `develop` in order; the next branch then rebases.

## The human approves commits and merges

The agent proposes; the human approves. Do not commit, push, or merge unless the human asked. Propose one focused slice and wait. A green build is not a commit, and an open pull request is not a merge.

## Pull request and release

PRs target `develop`. Rebase onto `origin/develop` first. The title includes `PSL-N`. The Test plan lists only steps that were run.

One area and one type on the Linear issue and the PR: `area-auth`, `area-dashboard`, `area-classes`, `area-ai-rag`, `area-infra`, `area-docs`, and `type-feature`, `type-bug`, `type-chore`, `type-tech-debt`. Not GitHub’s `bug` or `enhancement`. Assignee `raphaelmalims` if unset. Milestone is the current sprint, or `Backlog`. Request a reviewer other than the author when one exists. The PR body does not repeat those fields.

Before approve or merge:

- Walk every acceptance criterion on the GitHub Issue and on the Linear issue, and tick each met box on both. A review comment does not replace those checkboxes.
- Every listed Test plan step is `[x]`.
- CI is green.
- The Vercel preview is healthy.

Squash-merge into `develop` and delete the branch. Do not self-approve. Close the linked Issue as completed.

Promote `develop` to `main` with a merge commit, then tag `v0.x.0`.

Also ask before scope past the issue, before an untriaged Linear issue, and before a branch with no GitHub Issue.
